 plant called wolf's breath her  name's azula she's been working in the  garden since she was a teenager and it  seems like she might be important later  we check in with brother day who's with  the courtesan it gives us an insight  into how he experiences pleasure and  sexual satisfaction and a little bit  more about how their protective auras  work before he can satisfy his  physiological need for intimacy demarzel  interrupts because the proxima opal is  passed this is the leader of a religious  space and it sounds like a powerful one  considering it has trillions of  followers there's a potential problem  here because there's a new candidate who  has a chance to take over that follows  something called the primary octavia  this is a pre-imperial belief that  centers around individuated sentience  long story short as clones the cleons  could be viewed as less than human  brother day explains it to dawn he says  if the galaxy comes to believe that  their leaders are less than rather than  more than they may cease to follow so  there could be a legitimate threat to  their power and brother dusk plans to  visit the conclave in person to address  the situation even though all this time  has passed since the starbridge attack  on trantor they're still unrest and we  see there's an uprising in the lower  levels from the heatsink workers and the  cleons also learn about a communications  buoy going offline in the outer reach  this prompts brother day to bring up  terminus and the exile of harry selden's  followers there they have problems with  the conclave there's unrest at home and  now there's problems in the outer reach  he asks his brothers if they're starting  to see a pattern forming harry selden  laid out these very problems that  they're facing now and at that time  brother day didn't do anything about it  because he saw him as a charlatan so  there's a rift forming between day and  dusk the older has a reason to stick to  what he did back in the past even in  light of all these new events starting  to look like harry's predictions are  coming true  the current brother day summons the  royal master statisticians to ask them  about what they've learned about harry  sultan's math they've been working on it  for three decades now and still don't  really understand it they believe the  predictive models are counterfactual  because since he made his predictions  the empire has expanded rather than  contracted in every meaningful metric  when pressed though they can't say that  there's a non-zero chance that he isn't  right about everything in frustration  day goes and calls out dust for his past  mistakes with an acrion thespis and  terminus he says he's not going to let  him make the same mistakes and says that  he'll go to the conclave instead  demerzel steps up and interjects that  the primary cleon has never left trantor  at any time in the genetic dynasty but  she isn't able to change his mind so  dusk throws it out there that his  brother is haunted by selden's ghost and  then he's sent back to trantor where he  summons someone to go investigate the  boy going dark in the outer reaches and  he tells him that the dispatches from  the foundation have become sporadic pay  them a visit and tell them the empire  won't be kept in the dark so they'll be  heading to terminus we visit there and  pick up with salvor who ran into those  enactions in the remains of the slow  ship they've been on the planet for a  while scouting and their story is that  they're looking for the navigation  module from the ship they get salvor to  take the leader through the fence  because she wants to go to the tower in  the center of the city it works out that  she's only able to get the one person  through so the others tell her if she  doesn't return in the time a watch is  passed they'll raise the city to the  ground on the way salvor has another  vision and makes a move towards the  vault where the gnawfield knocks her  captor out she takes her prisoner and  figures out that she's the grand  huntress which gives them leverage they  can't really decide what to do with her  and salver thinks they need to get ready  to defend themselves she tries to get  information out of pharah because she  believes the navigation module is just a  distraction she shows her that she can  predict the outcome of coin flips to  sort of psych her out and through the  scars she has in her fake eye puts it  together that she must have been five or  six when she survived the empire's  attacks on her planet salvor realizes  where her resentment against the empire  comes from it's from losing her mother  and her brother and she tells the others  that she senses a deadness inside her  that she wants everyone to die  salvor talks to the encyclopedist louis  parine and you get a better  understanding of why he disregarded her  in the last episode this idea he has of  her being an outlier comes from the  connection to the bolt which he says is  something that couldn't have been  predicted through psycho history after  all it can't account for individuals  he goes to talk to pharah who mostly  ignores him and this insistence he has  that they're backed up by the empire she  says all of them have been exiled and  they're all dying just at different  speeds and she points out that harry  prophesied that the fall would begin at  the edge of the galaxy in their  conversation it starts to become clear  that they destroyed the buoy and landed  on terminus to get a response from the  empire they're just trying to provoke  them but it isn't clear what they're  after or why they think they have a  chance against them the people on  terminus start to realize that there's a  lot of an acronym surrounding the city  and when silver goes outside she has a  different kind of vision this one's  pretty vivid she's in the imperial  library and almost looks like gail at  least the clothes she's wearing and she  sees the boy with rach's knife again  she's able to talk to him this time and  says i won't hurt you just tell me who  you are and there is no answer and all  of that starts to convince her that it's  coming from the vault she tells hugo  this he says that she's special and that  he has absolute faith in her  pharah starts to convince lewis to help  her by telling him that they are  technologically bankrupt ever since  their atmosphere was set on fire she  continues the story that they need the  navigation module because they have  ships but can't make their way to a  different system to rebuild their  civilization as salvor's watching the  troops outside the fence assemble a  weapon she thinks there's a larger  strategy at play here but she can't  figure it out the vault isn't an acronym  or alien at all she believes it's from  harry but she has this crisis of faith  that maybe lewis is right maybe her  being an outlier is the reason that  things are going wrong and maybe the  visions are warning her to stay away  hugo counters this by saying what if you  are seldon's plan which i guess you  can't blame him for not understanding  how this works and picking up on the  fact that there is something going on  with salvor we leave them and in the  closing moments we see the cryopod  holding gale moving through space and it  approaches what looks like a spacecraft  as it cuts to black and the episode ends  there so there's a couple of things  happening on trantor something's up with  the new brother dawn brother day is  starting to think of harry selden's  predictions again in light of the new  crises that are emerging and brother  dusk is trying to defend the decisions  he made 35 years ago it's interesting  but it feels like it's taking its time  getting wherever it's going the  religious angle is essentially brand new  so i'm not sure what to expect with day  heading to the conclave the terminus  side of things is mostly the same as  last week the enacrions are there  there's a split in how they should move  forward salvor is having visions and i  wish i could say it got more compelling  as we're watching it unfold but this  episode didn't feel like a big leap  forward the thing that's most  interesting here for me is what happened  to rach gail and harry and it all kind  of undercuts the current events salvor  brings it up in this episode when she's  arguing with louis that harry says the  foundation survives the first crisis and  that makes all the running around in  circles a lot less dramatic i felt a  sense of relief when brother dusk  ordered the guy to go to terminus  because i think salvor is probably  correct that that's what an acrion is  trying to do so let's get there there's  a problem baked into a story that's  built on psycho history how do you make  it exciting when someone already figured  out how the future is going to play in  the beginning azimoth jumped from one  crisis to the next until it got  predictable and then he found different  ways to mix things up there were  different scenarios that came up as the  new civilization was developing the tv  show seems content to take its time and  present a lot of mysteries along the way  but even though everything's connected  it doesn't always feel like it so it's  promising to see that we get a glimpse  of gail here at the end because maybe  understanding what's going on there will  add to what's happening on terminus give  it a feeling it's going somewhere the  ideas of belief and faith are all over  this episode you have the populace's  belief in the genetic dynasty you have  that being backed up by the religious  leaders the cleon's faith in their  purpose and the encyclopedist faith in  harry selden all of that is being called  into question and then you have salvor  she's on the opposite side of the people  on terminus she's not so sure how she  feels about just sitting back and  believing that harry's plan would have  figured this all out but then she's also  having this personal crisis of faith  that's getting in the way of her moving  to try to figure out what to do with the  enacrion hopefully next week we'll see  how that plays out and what that'll mean  for the rest of the season last week i  decided to hold off on doing another  book to show video because i thought  there would be a lot of overlap with  this week there's a moment in episode 4  where salvor uses the saying that the  character is best known for in the books  violence is the last refuge of the  incompetent it's both a nod to the  source material but also kind of a wtf  moment because it points out how  different the show's version is so i'll  get into that in my next video i'll  discuss the changes that have happened  in episodes three and four and what i  think it means for how the story is  going to play out because i do think  this is a good place to leave this one  so let me know in the comments what you  think's going on what you're hoping to  see please like this video if you  enjoyed it please subscribe to my  channel if you haven't already thanks  for watching i'll talk to you soon

